+# assets/source/maps
+
+`slice-sea.tmj` is the slice sea (§3, §18 stage 2), a Tiled JSON map. It uses only the subset documented in `packages/content/src/tiledMap.ts`:
+
+- orthogonal, finite, 16 × 16 px tiles;
+- one embedded tileset (`firstgid` 1) whose tiles have a `type`: `sea`, `land`, `shoal` or `dock`. The art is placeholder colours drawn by the game, so the tileset has no image;
+- a tile layer named `terrain`, stored as a plain array of tile ids, every cell filled;
+- an object layer named `objects` with an `island` rectangle per island (on tile boundaries, named, string property `theme`: `tropical`, `volcanic`, `ruin` or `mist`) and a `spawn` point per spawn slot (int property `slot` from 0, string property `facing`: `E`, `SE`, `S`, `SW`, `W`, `NW`, `N` or `NE`).
+
+After editing, run `npm run map:build` from the repository root. It refuses a map outside the subset or one that fails the map validators (four islands with docks, shoals, reachable docks and slots, travel times), and writes `packages/content/src/maps/sliceSea.ts`. A unit test fails while that module is out of date.
